Z||000005||DXR_DAD||11-22-2000||12:35 AM||||Thanks Terry, Just didn't know the color name<BR>and the model it came on. Now what about that dark gray? it's on my 84 parts cars. What other year and model was dark gray?<P>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||6
Z||000006||tgowens||11-22-2000||01:38 AM||||well Bill, as far as I can remember, the '84 and '85 had the light gray, the '86 and '87 had a darker gray, and the '88 had an even darker gray. Same with the tan, '84 and '85 with a lighter tan than the '86 and '87 and the '88 had an even darker tan. But, I could be wrong.........just going by our parts cars over here.......the dashboards were basically the same color throughout the model years but the console, shifter surround and radio surround as well as the auxiliary guage surround were different shades to match the headliner and seat fabrics........but, what do I know - all of mine are '87's...<P>------------------<BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                              <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000007||RossT||11-22-2000||01:57 AM||||My fiero spotter's says for gray:<P>84,85  light slate gray<BR>86,87  dark gray<BR>88     medium dark gray<P><BR>84,85  medium doeskin<BR>86,87  light saddle<BR>88     medium beechwood||||reg||1
